  "junit_sha256": "248cdd5de0ed96f970d52b77a3db85f45b53ef553c82905959f9a98ba92b0e20",
  "priority_policy": "SetJournal sets registry name/conventional size. Later SetSize/tex_size wins for geometry. Active journal rc-font/linewidth keys override theme rc-fields regardless of action order; clearing journal(None) keeps current size and exposes explicit theme font fields. tex_size assigns separate body/label/title/tick sizes, so changing only body size is not changing explicit label_size.",
  "doc_change": "The older generic API doc said later fonts stick; it conflicted with existing registry override implementation. Clarified actual legacy priority and clear-journal behavior instead of adding new override flags/state or changing scientific preset calibration. No renderer/reducer behavior change.",
  "limits": "5actual repository TeX presets\u00d7columns1/2\u00d7fraction.75/1;4journal priority controls. Registry numbers are typical defaults, not a fresh official publication-guideline certification. PNGallows1pixelquantization; vectors checked72points/inch, TeXconversionuses72.27. No allDPI/UI/long-title/fallback guarantee.",
  "qa_control_note": "Initial test assumed bodyfont size15 overrides an explicit tex_size label_size; it did not. Set label_size15 explicitly to test intended per-field/journal priority. Not a renderer bug or an implementation priority change.",
